From: Fabien Danieau <fabien.danieau@pollen-robotics.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rk3566-radxa-zero-3w-aic8800ds2: restore chosen/bootargs

rk3566-radxa-zero3.dtsi includes rk3568-linux.dtsi and then does
`/delete-node/ chosen;`, removing Rockchip's bootargs. That is right for
radxa's U-Boot, which passes a cmdline from extlinux.conf, and wrong for
meta-rockchip's rk3568_defconfig U-Boot, which boots the Android boot.img
with an empty header cmdline.

Recreate the node with rw rootwait, console=ttyFIQ0 for bring-up serial and
console=tty0 for HDMI. earlycon is deliberately left out: it targets UART2,
the motor bus.

It deliberately carries no root=. U-Boot's RAUC boot script passes
root=PARTLABEL= for the slot it picked, and U-Boot merges this node into its
bootargs afterwards with a replace-same-key rule, so a root= here would pin
every boot to one slot regardless of the script. An earlier revision carried
root=PARTUUID=614e0000-..., from before the script existed.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [configuration]

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3w-aic8800ds2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3w-aic8800ds2.dts
@@ -12,6 +12,33 @@
 / {
 	model = "Radxa ZERO 3";
 	compatible = "radxa,zero3w-aic8800ds2", "radxa,zero3", "rockchip,rk3566";
+
+	/*
+	 * rk3566-radxa-zero3.dtsi does `/delete-node/ chosen;` right after including
+	 * rk3568-linux.dtsi, dropping Rockchip's bootargs because radxa's own U-Boot
+	 * passes them from extlinux.conf. meta-rockchip's U-Boot does not, so the
+	 * node is recreated with what we need:
+	 *
+	 *   rw rootwait      no initramfs; wait for the SD card to enumerate
+	 *   console=ttyFIQ0  serial during bring-up; when MICRODUCK_MOTOR_UART=1
+	 *                    disables the FIQ debugger the device never registers
+	 *                    and nothing is printed on the Dynamixel wire
+	 *   console=tty0     the HDMI console microduck-common.inc promises in
+	 *                    motor-bus mode; naming ttyFIQ0 alone would drop it
+	 *
+	 * Deliberately NO root=. U-Boot's boot script picks the RAUC slot and passes
+	 * root=PARTLABEL=rootfs_a|b in its bootargs env var; this node is merged into
+	 * that afterwards, and a same-key argument REPLACES rather than appends
+	 * (env_update_filter, cmd/nvedit.c). A root= here would silently pin every
+	 * boot to one slot whatever the script chose. It used to carry
+	 * root=PARTUUID=614e0000-..., from before any script existed.
+	 *
+	 * No earlycon: uart8250,mmio32,0xfe660000 is UART2, the motor bus, and it
+	 * bypasses the FIQ switch.
+	 */
+	chosen {
+		bootargs = "rw rootwait console=ttyFIQ0 console=tty0";
+	};

 	wireless_wlan: wireless-wlan {
 		compatible = "wlan-platdata";
